    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "An upload, end to end",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "\n- **Path**: browser → API endpoint (multipart, checks size/type) → **file service** (`POST /files`, service token, organization from the signed claim) → upload inspector → RustFS bucket `documents` under `{organization}/{ownerKind}/{ownerId}/{fileId}` → `files.StoredFile` row → the API records the `FileId` on the domain.\n- **Healthy**: *Rejected %* low and explained by *Rejections by reason*, no 5xx, S3 P95 in milliseconds, every health check green.\n- **Rejected ≠ broken**: the inspector refusing a file is a 400 with the reason. A 503 in the API means the file service or RustFS did not answer - see *Seen from the API* and *S3 errors*.\n- **Trace**: an upload is one trace across `hr-api` and `hr-file-service` with the S3 `PutObject` span inside - [Rootprint → Traces](http://localhost:8282/traces).\n- Traffic: `./infrastructure/start.sh --files` (avatars, about one in ten with a mismatched extension).\n"
      },
      "id": 33,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 54
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      }
    }
